# ⭐ ⑥ NOW HAS A FOURTH ELEMENT, and it is PRE-REGISTERED (cell gave it, next sharpened it):
#   ancestry + range + tree prove the right BYTES ARRIVED. They do NOT prove the landing DID THE
#   THING. So a warrant may name a PROPERTY checkable from the PUSHED TREE, with a control that
#   makes its zero non-vacuous — and it must be named BEFORE the tree exists, because a property
#   named at verification time is one chosen in the presence of the answer.
# ⛔ AND THE UNIT MATTERS MORE THAN THE PATTERN: next's first draft of a property counted TEXT HITS
#   and would have been RED ON A CORRECT TREE — the single hit was its own comment recording the
#   change. Ask the warranting door what the unit is; do not infer it from the name.

# ⛔⛔ MY OWN ROSTER WAS THE HOLE: I tracked WHO WAS DISPATCHED, not WHO STARTS BEAMs. A door can be
#   "free by ranking" and still be the heaviest user of the box. ⇒ THE QUESTION IS NOT "is this door
#   on a round I granted" BUT "does this door's landing script start BEAMs" — and it is answered by
#   asking the door, once, not by inferring from its repo.
# ⭐ AND A PER-START LOAD READ CANNOT CLOSE IT (chit and cell, independently): "two local SAFEs
#   cannot see each other." A sample answers "is the box busy NOW", never "is someone ABOUT to
#   start" and never "has someone been GRANTED it". That is why the window is a message from me.

